    <string name="rules_title">Rules</string>
    <string name="welcome_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="rules_1">Tiles slide inside the box. Never lift them out.</string>
    <string name="rules_2">The red one is Cao Cao. Get him out through the gap at the bottom.</string>
    <string name="rules_3">The little soldiers are the key. Don\'t just stare at the red one.</string>
    <string name="rules_mistakes">Common slips</string>
    <string name="mistake_1">No lifting, no jumping. Tiles only slide into empty space.</string>
    <string name="mistake_2">Cao Cao only fits through the middle gap.</string>
    <string name="mistake_3">Move Guan Yu (the wide one) aside first. That\'s where the room is.</string>
    <string name="mistake_4">Took a lot of moves? Fine. Undo is always there.</string>
    <string name="rules_source">\"Heng Dao Li Ma\": 81 moves minimum (Gardner 1964). Named after Guan Yu letting Cao Cao escape at Huarong Trail.</string>
    <string name="rules_how">Pinch a tile and push it along the slot. Or tap a tile, then tap an arrow.</string>

